00:00:17.272 --> 00:00:18.483
Thank you so much!

00:00:18.483 --> 00:00:20.567
Welcome to BuzzFeed Taste Test Live.

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:22.401
I'm your host, Keith Habersberger.

00:00:22.401 --> 00:00:25.118
Tonight's show is all about nachos.

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:26.925
(cheers and applause)

00:00:26.925 --> 00:00:28.112
The thing about nachos is

00:00:28.112 --> 00:00:31.159
even a shitty nacho is
still a pretty good nacho.

00:00:31.159 --> 00:00:32.038
It's still a nacho.

00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:33.709
It's sort of like sex in that regard.

00:00:33.709 --> 00:00:34.577
(laughs)

00:00:34.577 --> 00:00:37.535
I'm not gonna spend a lot of
time comparing sex to nachos,

00:00:37.535 --> 00:00:40.208
I think you get that it's
all messy and we get that.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.089
But I wanna prove my
theory that even a cheap,

00:00:43.089 --> 00:00:45.091
average nacho, is still pretty okay.

00:00:45.091 --> 00:00:46.332
So our first taste test

00:00:46.332 --> 00:00:48.386
is of the cheapest, most average nacho,

00:00:48.386 --> 00:00:50.266
which is, of course, from 7-Eleven.

00:00:50.266 --> 00:00:52.245
Here to taste it live, right now,

00:00:52.245 --> 00:00:55.298
are BuzzFeed's very own,
Maycie, Jen, and Jordan!

00:00:55.298 --> 00:00:57.514
(cheers and applause)

00:00:57.661 --> 00:01:00.104
- Ooh! They don't look bad!

00:01:00.104 --> 00:01:01.802
- No. I can smell them already.

00:01:01.802 --> 00:01:02.668
- What do they smell like?

00:01:02.668 --> 00:01:03.650
- Do we just eat them, Keith?

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:05.656
- Yeah, you just eat them.
That's what you do with nachos.

00:01:05.656 --> 00:01:06.414
(laughs)

00:01:06.414 --> 00:01:07.868
It's a taste test show, Jen.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:10.622
- I hate this cheese.

00:01:10.991 --> 00:01:12.244
- I don't hate it.

00:01:13.382 --> 00:01:15.164
- Fakest cheese I've ever had.

00:01:15.164 --> 00:01:17.205
- It's a little plasticky,
the cheese is, but--

00:01:17.205 --> 00:01:18.371
- It's a lot plasticky.

00:01:18.371 --> 00:01:19.088
- It's not horrible.

00:01:19.088 --> 00:01:21.587
- It's not bad. It's perfectly adequate.

00:01:21.587 --> 00:01:23.553
- Jen is the only one who's into plastic.

00:01:23.553 --> 00:01:24.651
(laughs)

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:25.640
She's fine with it.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:27.053
- Even the chips don't taste good.

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.058
- When do you think you would actually

00:01:28.058 --> 00:01:29.056
eat these in real life?

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.892
- When I was drunk, I would eat them.

00:01:30.892 --> 00:01:31.934
(laughs)

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.519
- You know what, you guys
are absolutely right.

00:01:33.519 --> 00:01:35.269
When you're drunk is
the perfect time to have

00:01:35.269 --> 00:01:37.556
7-Eleven nachos and we
thought of that ahead of time,

00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:39.665
so why don't we bring out
three shots of tequila!

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:42.572
(cheers and applause)

00:01:42.941 --> 00:01:44.987
- Alright. Bottoms up, ladies.

00:01:46.278 --> 00:01:49.361
(cheers and applause)

00:01:50.747 --> 00:01:52.323
Alright, don't get too carried away.

00:01:52.323 --> 00:01:54.784
The thing is, we're actually
going to take you now to a room

00:01:54.784 --> 00:01:57.245
with more tequila and
you are free to drink

00:01:57.245 --> 00:01:58.336
as much of that as you like.

00:01:58.336 --> 00:01:59.996
Obviously, stay responsible with it.

00:01:59.996 --> 00:02:02.214
Then, we're gonna have you come
back at the end of the show

00:02:02.214 --> 00:02:03.999
and eat those same nachos

00:02:03.999 --> 00:02:06.543
and see if, maybe, you find
them more delicious, huh?

00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:07.512
- Great, great.

00:02:07.512 --> 00:02:10.307
(cheers and applause)

00:02:14.138 --> 00:02:15.478
- How was the tequila room?

00:02:15.478 --> 00:02:17.522
And I guess the cerveza room, as well?

00:02:17.522 --> 00:02:19.388
- Yeah, I got over tequila, so.

00:02:19.388 --> 00:02:20.851
- If you were this
drunk on a normal night,

00:02:20.851 --> 00:02:22.643
what time in the evening would it be?

00:02:22.643 --> 00:02:23.564
- Six?

00:02:23.564 --> 00:02:24.525
(laughs)

00:02:24.525 --> 00:02:25.605
- Jen!

00:02:26.275 --> 00:02:27.738
- You start early!

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:31.151
- I'm gonna go with, like, 9:30?

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:33.499
- Oh, I was gonna say, like, 2 P.M.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.290
Or, no! A.M.! A.M.! A.M.!

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.120
- It's okay. That's the tequila talking.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.127
Well, let's take it on home.

00:02:39.127 --> 00:02:40.749
Why don't you try, or retry,

00:02:40.749 --> 00:02:42.543
those 7-Eleven nachos, now drunk.

00:02:42.543 --> 00:02:43.542
- Wooh!

00:02:43.542 --> 00:02:47.178
(cheers and applause)

00:02:47.178 --> 00:02:48.966
- They're so beautiful.

00:02:48.966 --> 00:02:50.173
- They are so beautiful.

00:02:50.173 --> 00:02:52.793
- Are these the same nachos
or new 7-Eleven nachos?

00:02:52.793 --> 00:02:54.512
- Girls, I don't know. I've
been here the whole time.

00:02:54.512 --> 00:02:55.344
(laughs)

00:02:55.344 --> 00:02:56.766
I think they're actually new.

00:02:56.766 --> 00:02:58.397
